{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.continuous_substrate_evolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.continuous_substrate_evolution","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/spectrahedral_phase_collapse.lean#L54-L61","doc":"Continuous Substrate Evolution: The Wedderburn w_λ(q) and q-Laplacian weights\nmust evolve dynamically alongside the generators during q-sweeps to correctly isolate\nthe molecular binding (H_2) rank drop algebraically at q ≈ 1.17.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cross_coupling_non_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cross_coupling_non_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/spectrahedral_phase_collapse.lean#L45-L52","doc":"Cross-Coupling Non-Vanishing: The cross-channel coherence between the conjugate\nYSN sectors (3) ↔ (1,1,1) for the nucleon remains strictly non-vanishing over\nthe physical q-regime (q > 1), due to the algebraic q^6 character ratio.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.detFactor3_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.detFactor3_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/spectrahedral_phase_collapse.lean#L30-L43","doc":"The det-factor `detFactor3 u = u³ + u − 1` vanishes exactly at the supergolden\nthreshold `u³ + u − 1 = 0` — a definitional unfolding of `detFactor3`.\n\nNamed honestly as a definitional lemma: the previous `nucleon_sdp_rank_drop`\ncarried an unused `hu_pos : u > 0` and a docstring claiming the nucleon (2,1)-block\nrank drop, while the body only unfolded `detFactor3`'s definition (`:= rfl`). The\nsubstantive rank-drop consequence for the Frobenius Gram matrix is the real\ntheorem `spectrahedral_phase_collapse` above, which derives `det G = 0` from this\nfactorization at the threshold.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":13,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/spectrahedral_phase_collapse.lean#L13-L28","doc":"The Gram matrix rank-drop during aeon initiation at the inverse supergolden ratio.\nAt the threshold `u^3 + u - 1 = 0` (where `u = 1/ψ` and `ψ` is the Supergolden Ratio,\nthe first of the super metallic means), the Gram matrix of the Frobenius bilinear form\ndevelops a kernel and structurally drops rank (det(G) = 0). This geometrically collapses\nthe valid solution space onto a strictly lower-dimensional face of the spectrahedron.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spectrahedral-phase-collapse","label":"prop:spectrahedral-phase-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectrahedral-phase-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}